<br> <mat>£2*<t-yellow>4</t-yellow>= £<gap>8</gap></mat>"},{"b":"Answer:<br> <mat><t-yellow>4</t-yellow>/<t-purple>5</t-purple></mat> of £10 = £<mat><gap>8</gap></mat>","hint":{"text":"Even though this question involves money, we still use the same rules as before. To find the <i>non-unit fraction</i> of the number, <i>divide</i> the number by the <b>denominator</b> and then <i>multiply</i> your answer by the <b>numerator</b>. ","speaker":true,"autoplay":false}}]},{"trainer":"gapMulti","finishButton":false,"gapMode":"write","instruction":{"text":"Find the fraction of the number."},"textAlign":"center","shuffleAtoms":false,"soundMode":"a","image":{"image":"adobe_49191256_crop-2113-393-2781-2781","width":200},"atoms":[{"a":"There are <b>8</b> dogs in the park. <mat><b><t-yellow>3</t-yellow>/<t-purple>8</t-purple></b></mat> of them are Labradors. How many are Labradors?","b":"<b>Divide</b> by the <t-purple>denominator</t-purple>:<br> <mat>8:<t-purple>8</t-purple>=<gap>1</gap></mat>"},{"b":"<b>Multiply</b> by the <t-yellow>numerator</t-yellow>:<br> <mat>1*<t-yellow>3</t-yellow>=<gap>3</gap></mat>"},{"b":"Answer:<br> <mat><t-yellow>3</t-yellow>/<t-purple>8</t-purple></mat> of 8 = <mat><gap>3</gap></mat>"}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Fractions","path":"/../c-mat-3-gb/topic-05-fractions/topic","puid":"c-mat-3-gb/e2tzyn"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Fractions of Numbers","path":"/../c-mat-3-gb/topic-05-fractions/block-06-fractions-of-numbers/block","puid":"c-mat-3-gb/gc006u"},"mediaFiles":{"sounds":[{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Find the fraction of the number.","etag":"8cd6-11277"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Carly invited <b>10</b> friends to her birthday party.<br> <mat><b><t-yellow>2</t-yellow>/<t-purple>5</t-purple></b></mat> of her friends couldn’t come. How many friends didn’t come to Carly’s party?","etag":"5412-58752"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Even though this question involves money, we still use the same rules as before. To find the <i>non-unit fraction</i> of the nu